      "fold_selection": {
        "_comment": "MATH with a corpus-specific gate and a corpus-derived stratification ladder. tau=0.4404 is the 70th percentile of the teacher's entropy over the MATH student pool, which puts gate coverage at 29.7% -- the same coverage GSM8K gets from tau=0.0335. The fixed step ladder was set for GSM8K and is far too coarse here: MATH answers run to 122 steps, so an open top stratum let the entropy arm take its longest members and the arms ended up 2.35 steps apart inside a single fold. Deriving the ladder from the pool brings that to 0.74.",
